A `join` is one word naming how a paragraph's first Waypoint stands to the paragraph before it, never a sentence, from a closed set: `consequence` -- this paragraph follows from what the previous one established, `grounds` -- this paragraph gives the reason for what the previous one asserted, `contrast` -- this paragraph sets its matter against the previous one's, `elaboration` -- this paragraph carries the previous one's matter further or in more detail, `summary` -- this paragraph draws the preceding paragraphs together, or `none` -- this paragraph opens on its own matter and no connective is owed.
